  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>This coastal path links Saint-Cyr-sur-Mer to Bandol via a "sentier des Douaniers"-type path that follows the coast through Mediterranean garrigue scrubland, passing the Port d'Alon cove — a lovely stop protected by the Conservatoire du Littoral. Depending on the stretch chosen, allow between 6-7 km (Bandol ↔ Port d'Alon) and up to 12 km for the full route to the Port de la Madrague in Saint-Cyr.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>Municipal order no. 2023.04.515 of Saint-Cyr-sur-Mer, which regulates the Port d'Alon - Nartette site (owned by the Conservatoire du littoral), allows dogs throughout the site, kept on a leash. The only restriction concerns the cove: from 1 April to 30 September, the beach, the part of the maritime public domain and the area behind the beach are forbidden to dogs from 9am to 5pm. Outside these dates, they are admitted there on a leash. Category 1 and 2 dogs must also be muzzled and held by an adult. The Bandol side is consistent: Bandol Tourisme says animals are accepted, kept on a leash, and describes a path that sometimes runs along the cliff edge, with roots and frequent ups and downs.</p>
      <p>The distances announced by the tourist offices: 6.3 km (about 2 h) from Bandol to Port d'Alon, of which 3.5 km from Bandol harbour to Les Engraviers then 2.8 km from Les Engraviers to Port d'Alon, and 4 km (about 1 h) from Port d'Alon to Saint-Cyr via the sentier des Vignes. On the Saint-Cyr side, the office announces 11.5 km and 5 h for the whole path from La Madrague to Bandol. The ground is rocky, with shaded pine-wood stretches between Les Engraviers and Port d'Alon, but little shade elsewhere: bring plenty of water for your dog.</p>
      <p>Several sections are restricted. The path is closed by municipal order between Pointe Grenier and Pointe Fauconnière because of the risk of cliff instability (falling blocks), pending a diversion. Bandol Tourisme also specifies, in information updated on 31/03/2026, that the metal footbridge of the Athéna estate is forbidden because of the risk of a pine falling and that a small part of the start on the Madrague side remains closed. Follow the signs and ask the Bandol tourist office (04 94 29 41 35) or the Saint-Cyr one (04 94 26 73 73) before leaving. From mid-June to the end of September, access to forest massifs is regulated according to fire risk, and under red code E the cove is totally closed.</p>
      <p>Parking at the cove is paid every day from 8am to 5pm from 1 April to 30 September (upper car park: €5 for the day; lower car park: €10 for the day, or €5 from 2pm). Car parks also exist in Bandol (Casino, Central, Stade) and on the Saint-Cyr side near the Madrague harbour.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: outside 1 April to 30 September, your dog can go on the cove's pebble beach on a leash, at any hour, and the parking fees published by the office run only from 1 April to 30 September. The rest of the year, the path is also much cooler for him.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>Saint-Cyr-sur-Mer and Bandol, at the two ends of the path, each offer ways to extend the outing: the <a href="/en/fiche-dogwash-saint-cyr-sur-mer">dog wash in Saint-Cyr-sur-Mer</a> to rinse off your companion after the walk, and on the Bandol side, the <a href="/en/fiche-bandol">Bandol beach</a> or <a href="/en/fiche-hebergement-bandol">dog-friendly accommodation</a> if you're extending your stay in the area.</p>
    </div>

